; DB connection config consumed by Utils\Connectivity\Database.
;
; Sections are keyed by database name (the section header IS the database
; name), and the connector resolves a database to its [<dbname>] section:
;
;   $conn = Database::connectAs($dbname, $account)
;
; $account is this repo's single service account (declared in the shared
; srv/roles-<GUID> package): `simox` (read-write on the primary, read on the
; replica). The connector reads the password from the <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD key
; (uppercased account name + _PASSWORD); an empty value means a passwordless
; account. This repo is passwordless by policy — the security boundary is
; ZeroTier membership plus the source-IP host pin that the framework
; gen-service-accounts derives from etc/team.ini / etc/machines.ini.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only and is MANUALLY MAINTAINED by the
; consumer (private data: copied into etc/ as a real file by simox's
; bin/fetch-private-data in dev, shipped into the freshly swapped etc/ by the
; framework's DEPLOY_PRIVATE_FILES — see doc/system/private-config.md).
; There is no generator anymore: `ema create
; srv/<name>-<GUID>` provisions the database's own MariaDB instance and
; prints the [<dbname>] section (SERVER/PORT/MYSQL_UNIX_PORT) for the
; operator to record here (or `ema values <db>` recovers a lost record). The
; dev sandbox lives in var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini (generated by
; 'ema sandbox srv/<name>-<GUID>'), not here.
;
; The <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD keys are manual, consumer-side credentials (recorded
; here by hand; empty = passwordless). The framework gen-service-accounts
; reconciles the account (create + drop stale, role-based) against the shared
; srv/roles-<GUID> declaration but does NOT write these keys back — this file
; is the manual source of truth.
;
; Two databases: `simo0` is the writable primary and `simo1` is its read-only
; replica (replication is established by ema's replica build — see
; doc/system/replica-bootstrap.md). Each has its own section below; both carry
; the single `simox` password key (`simox` is ALL on `simo0`, SELECT on
; `simo1`, and the website reads `simo1` through the same account).
;
; Transport: the section is authoritative for the 'ema' CLI. When
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT is set, ema connects via that socket (root/unix_socket
; auth); otherwise it uses SERVER/PORT over TCP. The app layer
; (Utils\Connectivity\Database) reads MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from .env, not from
; this file, so in prod it stays TCP-only (.env is MYSQL_*-free).

[simo0]
SERVER=10.147.x.10
PORT=3307
SIMOX_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock

[simo1]
SERVER=10.147.x.11
PORT=3308
SIMOX_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
